        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Eight cards of embroidery silks, made by Brown, Davis & Halse, England, 19th century"@en , "Eight cards of sewing silk with straight sides and scalloped ends wound with twisted two-ply sewing silk. \n\nThe cards are inscribed in four different sets of type-face: 'BROWN, DAVIS & HALSE'S PATENT MANDARIN SILK. BY HER MAJESTY'S ROYAL LETTERS PATENT. GRANTED MARCH 26th 1855.'."@en ;
